us.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257rig-c18"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257rig-c18"],"id":"long.record-257rig-c18","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.86 (Cofinal returns of the greedy carry)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.86, p. 69, label record:257rig-c18","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Suppose that for every $N\\ge0$ there is $M\\ge N$ such that\n$$\n\\operatorname{ihc}(G,M)\\le B(M+1)\n       =2\\lfloor\\sqrt{M+1}\\rfloor+4.\n$$\nThen $G$ is infinite and $X_G(2)=1/2$. Unlike Theorem 6.84, this hypothesis bounds the actual greedy carry only at unboundedly many indices. It still concerns the same fixed support $G$, not independently chosen finite supports. Comparing this carry with the carry obtained by fixing a finite prefix introduces a contribution from later omitted ranks. No equivalence with the finite-support hypothesis of Theorem 6.75 follows without controlling that additional contribution. The hypothesis is not established.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257rig-c18","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257rig-c18","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-c18%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfCarryReachability.greedy_half_infinite_of_cofinalStripReturn%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-c18%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfCarryReachability.greedy_half_infinite_of_cofinalStripReturn%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.HalfCarryReachability.greedy_half_infinite_of_cofinalStripReturn"},{"deriv